---
/** Home-page background: the human story the work page does not tell. */
import { site, withBase } from '../data/site';

const linkedin = site.socials.linkedin;
---

<section class="section" id="about">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
    <h2 class="section-heading">A bit of background</h2>
    <div class="prose about-text">
      <p>
        I came to front-end development from the project side. After a few years as a travel
        consultant, I managed web projects in an agency, coordinating editorial, design and
        development teams. In 2016 I retrained as a JavaScript developer, and I've been building
        interfaces ever since. That first career still shapes how I work: I think about the people
        who will use what I build. It's the same reason I'm taking the RGAA accessibility
        certification: everyone should be able to use it.
      </p>
      <p>
        My full experience is on the <a href={withBase('/work')}>work page</a>. To talk about a
        project or a role, the easiest way to reach me is on{' '}
        <a href={linkedin.url} target="_blank" rel="noopener">{linkedin.label}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
